# Repo-wide ignores.
#
# Individual projects also carry their own .gitignore, but those only protect the folders that
# still have one. When a project is deleted its .gitignore goes with it and its leftover build
# output suddenly shows up as untracked - which is exactly what happened to custom-backends after
# the in-process backends were removed. Keep the build output rules here so they apply everywhere,
# including to projects that no longer exist.

# Visual Studio
.vs/
*.user
*.suo

# .NET build output
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
artifacts/

# Test results / coverage
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
coverage/
*.coverage
*.trx

# Azure Functions local settings - these hold connection strings, never commit them
local.settings.json

# Node
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# Packages
*.nupkg
*.vsix

# Storage emulator state, written by the integration tests
.azurite/
__azurite_db*.json
__blobstorage__/
__queuestorage__/
